<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Ways a citizen can take a break (RimWorld: JoyGivers_*.xml). Before these existed, Need_Joy.GainJoy had
    one caller in the whole of src/ - CompDrug - so the only recreation in this civilization was narcotics and
    every citizen sat at the recreation need's worst stage (-20 mood) from day two onward for ever. See
    docs/WORK-REGISTER.md 9a.

    THREE GIVERS, AND ALL THREE NEED NOTHING BUILT. That is the point of this set rather than an oversight:
    a band that has just founded a settlement owns a knife and some rations, and a recreation system whose
    entries all require furniture would leave day two exactly as it was. RimWorld's own givers that need no
    building are Skygaze and GoForWalk; SocialRelax needs a gather spot in RimWorld and is translated here
    (see JoyGiver_SocialRelax's class doc for the translation and why it is the one taken). Building-based
    recreation - chess, horseshoes, art - is what a later pass adds on top; the field a building giver reads
    (thingDefs) already exists on JoyGiverDef.

    NUMBERS. baseChance and joyDuration could not be sourced against RimWorld's own JoyGiver content from
    this environment, so per CLAUDE.md they are stated here as what they are and the resulting BEHAVIOUR is
    pinned by test (tests/SimWorld.Core.Tests/AI/JoyTests.cs and
    tests/SimWorld.Core.Tests/Integration/SettlementMoraleTests.cs) rather than the literals:
      - joyGainRate 1 is RimWorld's own default and the unit JoyUtility.JoyGainPerTickAtRate1 is expressed in.
      - joyDuration 4000 ticks is one session; at rate 1 that is 0.576 of the bar before tolerance damping,
        so a citizen goes from "needs a break" to "had one" in a single session and not before.
      - baseChance orders the three: sitting with somebody is the common one, walking next, skygazing the
        rarest, and the social one is weighted highest because it is the only Social-kind giver in the set and
        a population that only ever took Meditative recreation would go bored of it (JoyToleranceSet).
  -->

  <JoyGiverDef>
    <defName>SocialRelax</defName>
    <label>relax socially</label>
    <giverClass>SimWorld.AI.JoyGiver_SocialRelax</giverClass>
    <jobDef>SocialRelax</jobDef>
    <joyKind>Social</joyKind>
    <baseChance>6</baseChance>
    <joyGainRate>1</joyGainRate>
    <joyDuration>4000</joyDuration>
    <canDoWithoutMap>true</canDoWithoutMap>
    <requiredCapacities>
      <li>Talking</li>
    </requiredCapacities>
  </JoyGiverDef>

  <JoyGiverDef>
    <defName>GoForWalk</defName>
    <label>go for a walk</label>
    <giverClass>SimWorld.AI.JoyGiver_GoForWalk</giverClass>
    <jobDef>GoForWalk</jobDef>
    <joyKind>Meditative</joyKind>
    <baseChance>3</baseChance>
    <joyGainRate>1</joyGainRate>
    <joyDuration>4000</joyDuration>
    <canDoWithoutMap>true</canDoWithoutMap>
    <requiredCapacities>
      <li>Moving</li>
    </requiredCapacities>
  </JoyGiverDef>

  <JoyGiverDef>
    <defName>Skygaze</defName>
    <label>skygaze</label>
    <giverClass>SimWorld.AI.JoyGiver_Skygaze</giverClass>
    <jobDef>Skygaze</jobDef>
    <joyKind>Meditative</joyKind>
    <baseChance>1</baseChance>
    <joyGainRate>1</joyGainRate>
    <joyDuration>4000</joyDuration>
    <unroofedOnly>true</unroofedOnly>
    <canDoWithoutMap>true</canDoWithoutMap>
    <requiredCapacities>
      <li>Sight</li>
    </requiredCapacities>
  </JoyGiverDef>

</Defs>
